    <string name="acoustic_quality_read_title">How to read it</string>
    <string name="acoustic_quality_read_axes">Up = higher pitch: bass at the bottom, cymbals at the top. The top is half the sample rate, the highest pitch the file can hold (22 kHz for 44.1 kHz audio). Left to right = time.</string>
    <string name="acoustic_quality_read_colour">Colour = how loud that pitch is, from black (silent) through purple, red and yellow to white (loudest).</string>
    <string name="acoustic_quality_read_cutoff">Real lossless music usually has sound almost to the top. If everything above one sharp line is dark, the file was probably made from an MP3 or AAC copy; those usually stop around 16–20 kHz.</string>
